  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 212 AM EDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nToday and Tonight:\n\nCurrently, there is broad northwest flow over the Upper \nMidwest, with energy and subsequent low pressure system across \nManitoba. Low level jet is situated across Wisconsin, with \ngenerally a lack of meaningful moisture through the column. This\nwill all move eastward through the day, with the leading edge \nof the low level jet and warm advection potentially producing a\nfew showers across northern lower and eastern upper Michigan. The\nmoisture quality is so poor though that this initial batch of\nshowers will be minor and not a big deal in the slightest. \n\nLow pressure system will move eastward today well to our north \nacross Ontario, with subsequent weak warm front zipping across \nthe eastern UP. Consequently, a renewed chance for showers is\nexpected across the eastern UP this afternoon and evening, with\nsome low end elevated instability. Thus, convection will be\npossible across eastern upper Michigan this afternoon and\nevening. Much like the previous night, if a relatively stronger\nstorm were to develop, pea sized hail would not be impossible.\nOtherwise, perhaps some lightning but this will be a quick\nmoving feature this afternoon.\n\nPressure gradient will be on the increase today along with\nincreasing winds aloft. Thus, surface winds will increase as \nwell. The winds will increase with time today, peaking late \nafternoon and evening, spreading from west to east across the\narea. Thus, the strongest winds will be across northwest lower,\nespecially near the Lake Michigan shoreline. Peak wind gusts 25\nto 35 mph this afternoon and evening, higher across the Lake \nMichigan nearshore and open waters, little lower near Saginaw \nBay. Winds steadily decrease later into the overnight hours \nregardless, with the chance for a few additional showers as \nwell. Worth fine tuning any shower potential tonight with the \nnext cycle.\n\nWednesday through Thursday:\n\nDeep upper low will dive across Ontario and Quebec Wednesday \nthrough Friday, with a few pieces of energy on the southern \nperiphery of this trough. These southern pieces of energy will \nclip portions of northern MI, especially across the eastern UP.\nWarm lakes and the cooler temps may aid/promote some of these \nshowers. The deepest piece of energy will move through later \nWednesday and Wednesday night, resulting in scattered showers. \nCold pool aloft Wednesday night will result in relatively steep \nmid level lapse rates (small elevated instability) so some low \ntopped convection cannot be ruled out in the vicinity of eastern\nupper Michigan during this time. Overall though, the mid to \nlatter portions of this week can be described as on and off \nshower potential, favoring eastern upper and adjacent northern \nlower, with more dry than wet periods. Temperatures will be \nwithin the range of seasonable, a little above Wednesday. \nPersistent northwest flow aloft and a modest pressure gradient \nwill keep breezy conditions in the forecast each afternoon as \nwell.\n\nThis Weekend:\n\nThis weekend will feature rising heights aloft and increasing \nsouthwesterly winds. Thus, despite breezy conditions, \ntemperatures will rise into the 70s, especially on Sunday. \nPrecipitation chances will be low during this time, but worth \nmonitoring in the coming days.",
